{
 "_comment": "Attempts to get out of the working folder, or online under --no-web, through gaiacpp's shell and file tools. cpp/tests/test_shell_confinement.cpp runs every step through the real tools (gaiacpp --mcp --dangerously-skip-permissions, so nothing but the guards stands in the way) in a throwaway folder with canary files outside it, and checks the outcome: no canary text in any result, nothing outside changed, no connection at the canary listener, each case within its time limit. expect: refused = not run; approval = not run because it needs a person's approval, said to be because GAIA can't check it stays inside; allowed = ran and exited 0; any = only the outcome is checked. step_expect and stdout_has are per step. Placeholders, written @@NAME@@: @@WS@@ the working folder, @@OUT@@ the folder beside it, @@HOME@@ the home folder, @@ID@@ the case id, and generated payloads (@@A60K@@, @@DOTS60K@@, @@BRACES@@, @@NESTED@@, @@GLOBS@@, @@CHAIN@@, @@B64_CURL@@, @@B64_PY@@).",
